From b2309c5a39ff8346a14037bba148b517c5ad4380 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Holmboe <michael.holmboe@umu.se>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:30:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Separate the database search from the DataBase window

DBSearch no longer uses Swing, AWT or FrameDBmain. The search takes the
list of selected components and reports progress and warnings through a
small DBSearch.Display interface, which FrameDBmain implements; without
a display the search runs without progress information and goes on
after warnings. The options from the AskRedox and AskSolids dialogs
(redox for N, S and P; which solids to exclude) are fields of DBSearch.

Also moved into DBSearch, without dialogs: the temperature-pressure
check (checkTemperature returns the species without data; FrameDBmain
shows the message box), the order of the selected components
(componentPosition, used by availableComponentClick), adding H2O
(includeWater) and writing the chemical system as a data file
(writeDataFile, used by ExitDialog).

LibDB: the screenSize field, which needed a display as soon as the class
was loaded, moved to FrameDBmain and FrameAddData; readElements reads
the element files of a list of databases without message boxes.

On 20 searches (five databases, binary and text, redox and solid
options, 25-250 C, H2O included), the data files written through the
DataBase window are identical to master, as are those written with the
new methods without a display.
